WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV v3.0 — latency (45s) Narrator Julius

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.001
First, open methods make AI cheaper on older machines,

2
00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:07.171
yet shipped products adopt them after a delay.

3
00:00:07.611 --> 00:00:14.312
Second, paying for the computer hardware dominates task cost, far exceeding the price of plug electricity.

4
00:00:14.752 --> 00:00:21.664
Third, quarterly calendars slow deployment until automation tools cut switching costs and force faster adoption.

5
00:00:22.104 --> 00:00:27.262
Faster attention kernels took ten months to ship and speculative decoding took two years.

6
00:00:27.262 --> 00:00:34.508
Beyond engineering work, listed companies gate releases around quarterly earnings targets and multi-year server depreciation.

7
00:00:34.948 --> 00:00:39.039
Once open algorithms make raw computation cheap on older chips,

8
00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:44.884
sellers charge mainly for the pain of switching away—and automation tools erase that pain.
